title "Newtonian mechanics"
layout radial root=motion
page a3
font 8pt..36pt wrap=17em

style law color=#1565C0
style quantity color=#2E7D32
style consequence color=#6A1B9A

node motion "Motion" .law
| position, velocity, acceleration
| kinematics describes motion without its cause
node frame "Reference frame" .law
| coordinates and time measurements
| inertial frames support Newton's laws directly
node force "Net force" .law
| interaction that changes motion
| vector sum of all external forces
node mass "Mass" .quantity
| resistance to acceleration
| inertial and gravitational mass are equivalent
node momentum "Momentum" .quantity
| p = m v
| vector conserved when net external force is zero
node energy "Kinetic energy" .quantity
| K = 1/2 m v^2
| scalar work changes kinetic energy
node potential "Potential energy" .quantity
| stored energy of position or configuration
| zero level is conventional; differences are physical
node first "First law" .law
| zero net force means constant velocity
| defines inertial motion
node second "Second law" .law
| F = m a
| acceleration follows the net force vector
node third "Third law" .law
| forces occur in equal and opposite pairs
| the pair acts on different bodies
node work "Work-energy theorem" .consequence
| net work equals change in kinetic energy
| W = integral F dot dr
node conservation "Conservation laws" .consequence
| momentum and energy constrain outcomes
| closed systems preserve total quantities
node gravity "Universal gravitation" .law
| F = G m1 m2 / r^2
| attractive inverse-square interaction
node orbit "Orbital motion" .consequence
| gravity supplies centripetal acceleration
| circular speed depends on mass and radius
node limit "Model limits" .consequence
| Newtonian mechanics fails near c or at atomic scale
| relativity and quantum theory extend the model

motion -> frame
motion -> force
motion -> momentum
motion -> energy
motion -> first
force -> second
mass -> second
force -> third
energy -> potential
force -> work
work -> energy
second -> conservation
third -> conservation
gravity -> orbit
mass -> gravity
second -> orbit
momentum -> conservation
energy -> conservation
conservation -> limit

require motion at center
prefer conservation at bottom-right weight=2
prefer limit near conservation within=18em weight=2
